// REJECTED — the Python/English word operator `and` is not revl syntax
// (item 384; syntax-2.0 §0/§3.3 exclusion diagnostics). `and` lexes as an
// ordinary identifier, so without a redirect it falls through to the generic
// G1 "`and` is not declared … declare it with `let`" — which actively
// misleads (it tells the author to declare a variable when the real fix is a
// different operator). The redirect names the idiom and the revl spelling.
//
// expected error:
//   use `&&`

fn f(a: Bool, b: Bool) -> Bool {
  return a and b
}
